   274	### 3.4 Trusted computing base
   275	
   276	The following are trusted, and a defect in any of them defeats the profile:
   277	
   278	- the installed manager parent, hardened supervisor, and domain-root worker
   279	  bytes, and the code that verifies their identities;
   280	- the domain session framing, authentication, nonce handling, and state machine;
   281	- the capability probes and the enforcement-backend adapters;
   282	- the operating-system or hypervisor primitives those adapters use;
   283	- the fingerprinted `go` launcher and the fingerprinted `GOROOT` tool
   284	  executables;
   285	- source and build-root canonicalization, fingerprinting, and input validation;
   286	- the operation-private roots, the artifact verifier, and the publication path;
